From Roger.Bivand at nhh.no  Fri Feb  6 15:02:03 2004
From: Roger.Bivand at nhh.no (Roger Bivand)
Date: Wed Nov 14 16:58:11 2007
Subject: [STATSGRASS] Fresh release (0.2-15) of R/GRASS interface on CRAN
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.44.0402062049340.15321-100000@reclus.nhh.no>

I do not usually advertise revisions of the R/GRASS interface - this time
is an exception, because it corrects a possibly serious and misleading
bug in displaying data within R. 

The plot method for grassmeta objects accepts a breaks= argument, but
until the present release, this argument was not being used in all
situations correctly by the underlying image() function painting the
raster values. This meant that when a legend was made using the assigned
breaks, the legend was correct, but the spatial distribution of painted
values was not necessarily so. How far they differed depended on the data.  

I believe that this bug is now fixed, but would welcome reports and
comments.

I apologise for any inconvenience,

Roger

